# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# --- bankferry: project-specific (merged in; the stock template above is unchanged) ---

# Editor/agent local state. The stock Editor/IDE lines above are commented out;
# activate the ones this project actually produces.
.idea/
.claude/

# Each binary is run from its own directory under cmd/ with its own .env, so
# every local artifact below may appear at the repo root OR under cmd/<name>/.
# Patterns are therefore unanchored unless they would otherwise match a
# source directory.

# Built binaries. The stock *.exe covers Windows; these catch the
# extensionless Unix/macOS builds. Anchored: an unanchored "bankferry" would
# ignore the cmd/bankferry source directory.
/bankferry
/brokerferry
/cmd/bankferry/bankferry
/cmd/brokerferry/brokerferry

# Local SQLite databases and their WAL/SHM sidecars, wherever a binary was
# run from. bankferry's holds the sync cursors; both hold the sealed
# production vault. Nothing in this repository is a committed .db.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Fetched and rewritten OFX files (OFX_OUTPUT_DIR; `map` writes to mapped/
# beneath it). Local financial data — never published.
ofx_output/

# brokerferry's investments snapshots (INVESTMENTS_OUTPUT_DIR, or wherever the
# operator pointed it). The .pb is the contract, the .json is the readable
# rendering of the same real holdings, the .part is one mid-write. None may
# ever be published.
investments_output/
reports/
investments_*.pb
investments_*.json
*.part
*.pb

# Encrypted credential backups and exports, under every name plaid-export has
# been given — local only, never published.
*.encryptedBackup
*.encrypted
*.tapb
access_token_backup*
# ...except the golden backup fixture: it holds fabricated tokens and is
# deliberately committed, so the format-regression test can read it.
!plaid/testdata/*.tapb

# Working migration checklist — never publish (removed once the move is done).
MIGRATION.md
